  "note": "Triennial election of Londonderry Corporation (aldermen and councillors), due Wednesday 21 May 1952: no contest. The twelve Unionist and eight Anti-Partition nominees were returned unopposed on nomination day, Wednesday 7 May (Derry Journal, 9 May 1952). The Journal's list gives the eight South Ward members as the Anti-Partition nominees and the North (8) and Waterside (4) members as the Unionist nominees. Swann replaced Alderman W. J. Little, who was not reselected by the Waterside Ward Unionist Association (Derry Journal, 7 May 1952). Returned unopposed."
